    "rated_by": "readiness",
    "rationale": "I rated it medium. The feature is read-only and shows no amounts. It does consume two new endpoints (E-PROJECTS, E-PROJECT), and the frontend must honour INV-ACCESS through \"no grant: 404\" without leaking the project title. It also changes the shared contract mock (`frontend/mock/server.mjs:24`, 226-234) while F-05, F-06 and F-08 change the same file (PMO-0-3), and it replaces a route that the frame tests assert on (PMO-0-4). Surfaces: - `ui`: SCR-22 and SCR-07. - `api`: the first reads of E-PROJECTS and E-PROJECT through the generated client and the mock. Excluded surfaces: - `payments`: the Money and Milestones tabs are split out. - `contract-change`: no repoint and no openapi edit. - `security` and `auth`: the page only renders 401, 403 and 404 through the existing mapping. - `product-decision`: the omitted elements are recorded for product acceptance, not decided here."
  },
