    {
      "id": "TECH-2-1",
      "round": 2,
      "snapshot_ref": "ab641e93900ddddcaeaa19d323f33fa9045ef9d0",
      "owner": "frontend",
      "severity": "medium",
      "blocking": false,
      "summary": "The proposal shapes the client reads are not type-guarded and differ from the v7 draft. Today they only reach the page from the mock, so nothing breaks. Once a backend serves v7, `ProjectsList.tsx:97` (`item.next_milestone ?? '\u2014'`) would render an object `{name, due}` as a React child and throw. `ProjectJourney.tsx:117` would print \"PM [object Object]\" because v7 `pm` is `{name, role, is_you}`. v7 `facts` is an array of `{label, value, money, unknown}`, but the client reads an object, so the strip shows \"Not known\". v7 `summary` is `agent_summary` `{agent, text}`, and the line `tone` and `station` are new. The client should check `typeof` before rendering each proposal field (string for `next_milestone`, `pm` and the line text), so that an unexpected shape degrades to \"\u2014\" or \"Not known\" instead of throwing. When v7 is frozen, align `model.ts` and the mock fixtures to it. Under the standing rule this does not block the round.",
      "reproduction": null,
      "evidence_refs": [
